  "content": {
    "text": "Opening Bid's Stock of the day: Microsoft has slipped below its 200-day moving average. Yahoo Finance Executive Editor Brian Sozzi is joined by Crossmark Global Investments Chief Market Strategist Victoria Fernandez and Yahoo Finance Markets & Data Editor Jared Blikre to break down what's driving the weakness in the tech giant and how to play it going forward.\nwe've been underweight these Mag 7 stocks for a while. I mean, they're still some of our largest positions in our portfolio, but Microsoft is our largest underweight that we have. We've actually been trimming that name for a while, using those uh funds for other areas, but also starting to maybe nibble on some other software names and maybe just hold our Microsoft position where it is now. Like you said, it has come down so significantly that at this point in time, we're not adding to it, but we would hold it here. It's a good long-term hold.\nand earnings were good. You got revenues up what, 19%, cloud up 40%, earnings up 20%. I mean, these are good numbers. So I think you can hold it in your portfolio for a while, but there's just not going to be a lot of action here, uh moving the stock tremendously higher. Maybe use op or um, yeah, use options here, write some calls on this to maybe generate some cash flow off of any holdings you have.\nAnd I'm with you 100%. This is software itself has been disappointing over the since basically uh last October, November when it peaked. This is our mega caps. This is a trillion dollar club and the year-to-date performance, you can see Microsoft by far the worst off there. It's below Tesla, meta, which are also in the red. And let me just show you a chart. This is going to be a two year of Microsoft and I'm going to put a 200 day moving average in there. You just mentioned it.\nWell, we just broke above it for literally one day and then rug pull and everyone sold off. And so now we are back towards the lows of 2026 and also 2025 and that's a very important formation. Let me show you a 10-year chart now and I'll take that moving average off. This right here is a neckline of a potential, just a potential head and shoulders top. So 350 is my key line here.\nIf it breaks 350, all bets are off. I don't know that I'd want to hold this that long. Uh but as long as it stays above it, we still got some room to consolidate. But the remnants of the AI scare trade are alive and well. There's still a lot of doubts about uh AI kind of eating software's lunch and it's just the multiples are coming down. The earnings are great. Well, some of the earnings are great, but yeah, the multiples are coming down.\nJared, uh the head and shoulders pattern, is that bearish?\nWell, it is. If you break that neckline right there, it's called you take what's called a measured move. So you take the distance between the neckline and the top and then you subtract that from the neckline. So if that's $200 uh that you have consolidation, let's just say that's for, you know, argument sake, that's where we are, then it'll go down by an equal amount. So we're looking somewhere in the probably low 200s right there.",
    "text_blocks": [
